WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.980
Good morning to each and everyone present here.

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.400
I have a confession to make.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.660
I used to be heavily involved in underground trading.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.880
Sticker trading. Very serious business.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.260
Glitter was like the gold standard.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.040
I had this obsession with collecting stickers.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:23.380
You know the shiny ones that you'd beg your parents for at the stationery shops?

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.260
I had a whole box of them.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:30.780
Glittery stars, cartoon characters, even rare ones that I traded with friends.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.520
And every time someone asked why I never used them,

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.540
I'd say these are special.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.260
I'm saving them for a good occasion.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.960
But here's the twist. That good occasion never came.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.780
I held on to them for so long,

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:54.340
protecting them, waiting for the perfect moment to do something with them that I eventually grew out of

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:55.420
stickers altogether.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:02.200
They just sat there unused until one day I realized they weren't worth anything anymore.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.520
And that's when it hit me.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.600
Money works the same way.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.640
If you just collect it, stack it,

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:13.320
and wait for the perfect moment to do something with it,

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.520
you're just wasting its potential.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.840
Stickers don't grow in value when you hide them in a box and neither does money.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:26.060
However, the real wake-up call wasn't about those stickers.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.394
It was my dad.

00:01:28.774 --> 00:01:32.354
My father works harder than anyone I've ever known.

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:36.434
Long hours, late nights, never once complaining.

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:41.094
I have seen him wear the same pair of jeans for three years in a row because they

00:01:41.094 --> 00:01:47.694
still work fine while happily spending money on me if I so much as mentioned something in passing.

00:01:48.254 --> 00:01:50.054
Beta, do you need new books?

00:01:50.154 --> 00:01:50.714
Done.

00:01:51.154 --> 00:01:53.354
My little girl has her eyes on a new dress.

00:01:53.354 --> 00:01:56.714
Here's the money. Dad needs new shoes.

00:01:56.714 --> 00:01:58.514
Oh, these still have some sole left.

00:01:58.514 --> 00:02:05.714
And before him, my grandfather, a man who worked his entire life sun up to sun down,

00:02:05.714 --> 00:02:06.934
building a foundation for us.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:12.094
His generation's mantra was work hard and sacrifice.

00:02:12.154 --> 00:02:14.834
And he did every single day.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.954
And here's what I've realized.

00:02:16.954 --> 00:02:24.174
If my grandpa's generation was about working hard and my dad's generation was about sacrificing for the next,

00:02:24.174 --> 00:02:28.334
then my generation's responsibility is to work smart,

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:31.114
to build wealth, not just chase it.

00:02:31.114 --> 00:02:33.014
Because here's the truth.

00:02:33.154 --> 00:02:37.294
No matter how hard you work, if you don't know how to manage your money,

00:02:37.294 --> 00:02:39.194
it will slip through your fingers.

00:02:39.194 --> 00:02:41.594
The 50-30-20 rule.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:48.214
50% for needs, 30% for wants and 20% for your future self.

00:02:48.614 --> 00:02:50.594
And then there's compound interest.

00:02:50.594 --> 00:02:52.854
Einstein's 8th wonder of the world.

00:02:53.394 --> 00:02:55.828
If I invest 2,000 a month now,

00:02:55.828 --> 00:02:59.968
by 60 I'll have around 3.7 crores.

00:03:00.088 --> 00:03:03.728
If I wait till 25, barely half of that.

00:03:04.488 --> 00:03:08.348
7 years of delay costs me almost 4 crores.

00:03:08.468 --> 00:03:12.788
That's not mathematics, that's dark magic punishing procrastination.

00:03:13.708 --> 00:03:14.848
Now most of you all will say,

00:03:14.848 --> 00:03:18.308
we're not even adults yet, we don't have the money right now.

00:03:18.728 --> 00:03:25.328
Really, check your food delivery history or that one night you and your friends spent way too much

00:03:25.328 --> 00:03:27.148
on snacks.

00:03:28.008 --> 00:03:30.068
Fun gives you a moment.

00:03:30.308 --> 00:03:32.888
Investing gives you a lifetime.

00:03:33.488 --> 00:03:36.128
You don't have to be rich to invest.

00:03:36.128 --> 00:03:40.108
You have to invest in order to get rich.

00:03:40.568 --> 00:03:42.888
Allow me to tell you about this friend of mine.

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:45.028
She's like super rich.

00:03:45.348 --> 00:03:47.448
Her grandma gets the credit for her,

00:03:47.448 --> 00:03:51.088
if it's not designer, it's disposable mentality.

00:03:51.448 --> 00:03:58.128
Picture this, a young widow, eight kids and a house so chaotic it could register on the Richter

00:03:58.128 --> 00:04:00.948
scale. Most people would panic.

00:04:00.948 --> 00:04:03.748
But grandma, she looked at the chaos and thought,

00:04:03.748 --> 00:04:06.908
money, a plan and a miracle.

00:04:06.908 --> 00:04:10.108
Let's do all three. Step 1, budgeting.

00:04:10.268 --> 00:04:13.208
She borrowed money from her brother, not for a sari,

00:04:13.208 --> 00:04:16.528
not for television, but to buy cows.

00:04:16.528 --> 00:04:18.008
Every rupee was accounted for.

00:04:18.008 --> 00:04:21.588
If she so much as overspent on grass,

00:04:21.588 --> 00:04:23.528
it was a disaster.

00:04:23.862 --> 00:04:26.202
And that is your first lesson.

00:04:26.262 --> 00:04:28.682
Budget like your life depends on it.

00:04:28.842 --> 00:04:30.122
Because it does.

00:04:30.642 --> 00:04:31.662
Step 2. Investing.

00:04:31.662 --> 00:04:35.122
These cows weren't just cows.

00:04:35.342 --> 00:04:36.542
They were assets.

00:04:36.882 --> 00:04:39.322
Milk, ghee, yogurt.

00:04:39.482 --> 00:04:43.042
Every product multiplied her initial investment.

00:04:43.162 --> 00:04:48.942
She turned a simple loan into a cash-flowing business before she even knew the words ROI or

00:04:48.942 --> 00:04:52.782
stocks. Step 3, saving and financing wisely.

00:04:53.102 --> 00:04:59.562
Every rupee she earned, she saved and bought gold which covered her children's education and other expenses.

00:05:00.382 --> 00:05:05.362
By the end, she had created generational wealth all on her own.

00:05:05.542 --> 00:05:09.482
And honestly, if she can do it with eight screaming kids,

00:05:09.582 --> 00:05:15.702
I think we can survive budgeting our overpriced coffees and Uber rides that cost more than the actual

00:05:15.702 --> 00:05:16.662
event.

00:05:17.362 --> 00:05:22.322
Seriously, if you don't start now, you won't magically wake up one day knowing how.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:27.582
You'll just wake up older, with less time and the same fears.

00:05:27.622 --> 00:05:31.002
Stop telling yourself money is complicated.

00:05:31.002 --> 00:05:34.342
Stop waiting for the perfect moment.

00:05:34.482 --> 00:05:39.042
Stop promising your future self that you'll figure it out later.

00:05:39.042 --> 00:05:43.582
I would like to take your leave by sharing my favorite quote by Robert Kiyosaki,

00:05:43.582 --> 00:05:45.842
author of Rich Dad, Poor Dad.

00:05:46.262 --> 00:05:47.962
Don't work for money.

00:05:47.962 --> 00:05:50.442
Make money work for you.

00:05:50.802 --> 00:05:51.462
Thank you.
